"""
## Purpose and audience

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing UNIT-LIB behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/http_client/url_encode_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
# @manual: primary
# REQ-UNIT-LIB-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
# @req REQ-LIB-HTTP-URLENCODE-001
"""
# `url_encode` percent-encoding under the interpreter

**Category:** Stdlib
**Status:** Implemented

## Purpose and Audience

Anyone building a URL or query string from user data via
`std.nogc_sync_mut.http_client.types.url_encode`. This spec exists because
`doc/08_tracking/bug/interp_http_url_encode_utilities_unresolved_2026-06-14.md`
was closed with no surviving covering spec: `url_encode` used to be entirely
unusable under the interpreter, with the calling function dying silently after
`[WARN] Failed to load export source error=semantic: Cannot resolve module:
utilities`.

## Scope and Preconditions

Pure function, no host state. The original defect was a MODULE RESOLUTION
failure, so the load-bearing part of this spec is that the import resolves and
the function returns at all -- silent death, not a wrong value, was the
symptom. The value assertions guard the encoding itself.

## Primary Workflow

Encode strings containing characters that must be escaped in a URL, and confirm
unreserved characters are passed through untouched.

## Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Unreserved | `A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . ~` survive encoding unchanged |
| Percent-encoding | Everything else becomes `%HH` with uppercase hex |

## Related Specifications

- `doc/08_tracking/bug/interp_http_url_encode_utilities_unresolved_2026-06-14.md`
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.nogc_sync_mut.http_client.types.{url_encode}

describe "url_encode percent-encodes reserved characters":

    it "encodes the at-sign in an email address":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-001
            # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-002
            # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-003
        step("Verify: encodes the at-sign in an email address")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Encode the address from the original bug report")
        # This exact call is what used to die silently after printing CLIENT_OK.
        expect(url_encode("ops@acme.com")).to_equal("ops%40acme.com")

    it "passes unreserved characters through unchanged":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-004
        step("Verify: passes unreserved characters through unchanged")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Encode a string made only of unreserved characters")
        expect(url_encode("abcXYZ019")).to_equal("abcXYZ019")

    it "encodes a space":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-005
        step("Verify: encodes a space")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Encode a value containing a space")
        expect(url_encode("a b")).to_equal("a%20b")

    it "encodes characters that would otherwise break a query string":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-006
        step("Verify: encodes characters that would otherwise break a query string")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Encode the query delimiters")
        expect(url_encode("a&b")).to_contain("%26")
        expect(url_encode("a=b")).to_contain("%3D")

    it "returns an empty string for empty input":
        # @req: REQ-UNIT-LIB-007
        step("Verify: returns an empty string for empty input")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        step("Encode the empty string")
        expect(url_encode("")).to_equal("")
